  "title": "Paul H NDE 6528",
  "date": "03 December 2012",
  "content": "I was visiting New York on holiday and on the last day I had a condition called an Arrhythmia which is a life threatening irregular heartbeat, I was rushed to New York Downtown hospital where I was given a drip to try to regulate my heart rate. At approximately 1:00 a.m. I was given a drug, which I believe is supposed to stop and re-start the heart. My partner was sitting opposite me. He observed my eyes rolling back into my head so only the white was visible and my jaw went slack, leaving my mouth open. My personal experience was hearing the Doctor telling me 'this is going to feel a little weird'. The next thing I remember incredibly vividly is looking down and seeing myself on the stretcher. I felt a feeling of warmth, security and total peace. I could see myself somehow over trees, the experience was as if I was in a wonderful dream. Then I was resuscitated, my vision and mind became clear, and I realized where and what was going on. Had I died there? I can honestly say that I wouldn't have suffered in any way. However, for my partner the whole thing was horrific. But my personal experience was one of peace, security and love. For a person with absolutely no religious conviction I feel the experience was actually spiritual.",
